# CMake Conventions

Root project: C++20, extensions off, MSVC `/W4 /permissive-`, outputs under `build/bin` and `build/lib`.

## Targets (modern CMake)

- `SatRuntime` / `SatEditor` — libraries under `Engine/`; public includes from `Engine/*/include`
- `GamePlayer` — standalone executable that links `SatRuntime` privately
- Use target-scoped commands only — no global `include_directories` / `link_libraries` / `add_definitions`
- `PUBLIC` = part of the consumer API; `PRIVATE` = implementation-only; `INTERFACE` = header-only deps
- Prefer `PRIVATE` for third-party libs hidden behind wrappers (e.g. GLFW once fully wrapped)

## Dependencies

- Fetch with `FetchContent`; pin a tag; disable docs/tests/examples/install when unused
- Do not put third-party sources into public include paths unless they are part of the API

## When adding code

```cmake
# ❌ BAD — new .cpp missing from the target
add_library(SatEngine STATIC Core/src/Application.cpp)

# ✅ GOOD — every translation unit listed explicitly (including src/module/)
add_library(SatEngine STATIC
    Core/src/Application.cpp
    Core/src/Window.cpp
    Renderer/src/Renderer.cpp
    Renderer/src/module/MeshPass.cpp
)
```

- Expose public headers with `target_include_directories(... PUBLIC ...)` (`Engine/*/include`)
- Resolve private `src/module/` headers with `target_include_directories(... PRIVATE .../src)` — never PUBLIC
- Keep `target_compile_features(... PUBLIC cxx_std_20)` on the library
- Prefer `target_link_libraries` / `target_compile_options` over directory-wide flags
- Never hand-edit generated files under `build/`
- Configure/build via presets / `scripts/build.ps1`; do not invent a parallel layout
